-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(33453.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(34216.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(34605.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(35108.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(35611.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(35972.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(36250.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br><br>Hence, the statement (a) is true.<br><br>(b) The electrolysis of alumina by Hall-Heroult's process is carried by using a fused mixture of alumina and cryolite (Na<sub>2</sub>AlF<sub>6</sub>) along with minor quantities of aluminium fluoride and fluorspar. The addition of cryolite and fluorspar increases the electrical conductivity of alumina and lowers the fusion temperature. Hence, the statement (b) is true.<br><br>(c) At anode, alumina reacts with fluorine to liberate oxygen and evolved oxygen reacts with carbon to form carbon dioxide and hence, statement (c) is true.<br><br>(d) Steel cathode with carbon lining and graphite anode are used and hence, the statement (d) is true."
